sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor G as Giver (guest or signed in)
    participant SM as StoetModel
    participant RL as RateLimiter ("auth")
    participant RC as IRecaptchaVerifier
    participant IS as IInboxStore
    participant DB as MarsvinDb
    participant ES as IEmailSender
    actor ST as Staff

    Note over G,ES: A public form. A money donation is a demo like the checkout:<br/>it is recorded, never charged, and no card details are asked for.

    G->>SM: POST /Stoet (kind, amount or item description,<br/>name, email, greeting, captcha token)
    SM->>RL: 50 requests per minute per IP?
    alt over the limit
        RL-->>G: 429 Too Many Requests
    else within the limit
        alt Money: amount missing or outside 10 - 10,000 kr.
            SM-->>G: Page() with the field marked
        else Products: description, name or email missing
            SM-->>G: Page() with the fields marked
            Note over SM: Only the fields of the chosen kind are required -<br/>a money donation may be anonymous.
        else valid
            SM->>RC: VerifyAsync(captcha token)
            alt captcha rejected
                SM-->>G: "Bekraeft at du ikke er en robot"
            else captcha ok
                SM->>IS: AddDonation(donation)
                IS->>DB: INSERT Donations
                Note over SM,DB: Only the fields that belong to the chosen kind are kept,<br/>whatever else the form posted.

                opt an email address was given
                    SM->>SM: IsEnglish()? - the marsvin-lang cookie of this request
                    SM->>ES: SendAsync(donor email, "Tak for din donation til Marsvin"<br/>or "Thank you for your donation to Marsvin")
                    Note over SM,ES: Fixed wording: the amount, or the shop's address and opening hours.<br/>The donor's own free text (what they offer, their greeting) is NOT repeated,<br/>and the name is kept to one line - the address is whatever was typed in,<br/>so the form must not become a way to send a stranger your own wording.
                    alt sending failed
                        Note over SM: Logged only. The donation is already saved,<br/>so the giver still sees the thank-you and a retry<br/>cannot become a second donation.
                    end
                end

                SM-->>G: Redirect to /Stoet with a thank-you toast
            end
        end
    end

    ST->>IS: GET /Admin/Donations (Admin or Employee)
    IS->>DB: SELECT the most recent donations
    IS-->>ST: list - amount or items, name, email, greeting

    Note over G,ST: An anonymous money donation sends no mail - there is nobody to write to.
